-- title:
--   Index of ±Γ_H(q²M') for H the kernel mod q
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $3 \le q$, and let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$. Write $N = q^2M'$, and let `levelH q M'` be the subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ given by the kernel of the reduction homomorphism `ZMod.unitsMap` attached to $q \mid q^2M'$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let [`CohCarrier.GammaH N (levelH q M')`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained as the image, under the inclusion of $\Gamma_0(N)$, of the preimage of that subgroup under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ sending a matrix to the class of its lower-right entry; concretely, the matrices in $\Gamma_0(N)$ whose lower-right entry is $\equiv 1 \bmod q$. The assertion is that twice the index in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the subgroup generated by this $\Gamma_H$ together with $-1$ (the join with the cyclic subgroup `Subgroup.zpowers (-1)`) equals $q(q^2-1)\,\psi(M')$, where the subtraction is in $\mathbb{N}$ and $\psi(M') = \sum_{d \mid M',\ d \text{ squarefree}} M'/d$ is `dedekindPsi`.
--
--   This is the computation of the index of $\pm\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$, equivalently of the index $\mu = q(q^2-1)\psi(M')/2$ in $\mathrm{PSL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the congruence subgroup carrying full level-$q$ structure over $\Gamma_0(M')$. It feeds the genus formula for the corresponding modular curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, being cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_fieldBar_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_fieldBar_eq) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_fieldBar_eq_of_eq_three`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.genusFF_fieldBar_eq_of_eq_three).
-- source:
